The architecture baseline was copied from a chat answer and its
rendered page. It still opened with the chat reply, carried interface
labels such as "图表选项", "YAML" and "运行" in front of code blocks, and
its three diagrams did not render: one pointed to a PNG on a local
disk, and two were mermaid output inlined as SVG data URIs, which
GitHub does not display and which made up more than half of the file.

Replace the chat reply with a short statement of what the document is,
drop the interface labels in favour of language tags on the code
blocks, and redraw the three diagrams as mermaid source (the two SVGs
are decoded node for node; the overview follows the layers of 3.1).
The front matter said the body was copied unmodified from a file on a
local disk, which stopped being true with ADR-013; it now says that
this file is the source of truth, and a revision record at the end
lists the changes.
